  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Explain how the graph of $y=\\log_2(8x)$ can be obtained from the graph of $y=\\log_2x$ by either a translation or a dilation.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Translate $3$ units up, or dilate horizontally by factor $\\tfrac18$ from the $y$-axis.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2(8x)&=\\log_2 8+\\log_2x\\\\\\log_2(8x)&=\\log_2x+3\\end{align*}$$\nThus translate $y=\\log_2x$ three units up. Alternatively, replacing $x$ by $8x$ gives a horizontal dilation of factor $\\tfrac18$ from the $y$-axis.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 25
  },
